WEBVTT

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:17.450
On the bus is number one, part one, production number 0157, recording date 14269, take one.

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:32.850
Over is our thieves!

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:15.680
All these new schedules are murder, aren't they?

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:18.260
Don't you happen to get up this time in the morning?

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:20.150
No morning papers.

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:25.580
Look at that, even Tony Blackburn ain't up.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.440
They're breakfast, eat it up.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.100
I'm not going to need it in me socks, Mum.

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:32.060
Where's me shoes?

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:33.020
I put them here last night.

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:33.780
I've got them here.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:35.980
They're in the oven to keep warm.

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:40.500
Tell her, love.

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:41.160
Here you are, love.

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:43.240
I don't know what they wanted to order them for.

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:44.840
They was all right as they were.

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:45.240
Oh!

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:47.840
What did I say?

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:49.300
Are you all right?

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:50.260
Are you all right?

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.100
Yeah, next time, give her another five minutes

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:54.040
and number six and send a recipe to Jimmy Young.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:57.140
Now, look here, Stan.

00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:59.120
You're going right through the soul again.

00:01:59.380 --> 00:01:59.880
Oh, my God.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.940
Nope, it's the brake pedal that does it.

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:03.620
Well, you shouldn't press it down so hard.

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:04.400
Don't be darned.

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:06.320
If I don't press it down so hard, I'll go right through a brick wall.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:08.880
Come on, come on, eat up your breakfast.

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:10.280
You're looking very pale, you know.

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:11.300
Oh, turn it in, will you?

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:13.260
Just the same when you was a lad.

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:16.120
Always, always pale-faced and thin.

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:18.320
Mum, Mum, can I have a cup of tea, please?

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:19.880
Yes, of course, of course.

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:20.180
Thank you.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:21.460
There we are.

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:27.020
Just because you're on the early shift, you don't have to get the old house older.

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:29.610
Me and Olive have been up since five o'clock.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.280
Oh, I'm sorry about that.

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:32.780
Oh, you didn't bother to have come down.

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:34.320
Stan would have got you a nice cup of tea.

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:36.460
He married my sister, not me.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:39.840
Yeah, well, since I'm up, I'll have me breakfast.

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:40.900
Yeah, well, you have to wait, dear.

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:42.700
I've got to get Stan's lunch ready first.

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:44.180
Stan's lunch?

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:46.200
I thought you always had it in the canteen.

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:47.900
I did, but with these new schedules,

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:49.420
I'm never back in the depo in time.

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:50.660
You stand for that.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:53.380
Every man is in type of canteen facilities.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:54.980
Your union should have done something about it.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:55.660
They did.

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:56.890
They agreed.

00:02:57.520 --> 00:02:58.380
I suppose you was...

00:02:58.380 --> 00:02:59.980
I suppose you was too...

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.840
trying to stand up at the meeting and say anything?

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:03.040
Oh, no, I wasn't.

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:04.650
Why don't you speak up for yourself?

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:05.760
I wasn't there.

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:08.090
It was my bingo night.

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:09.600
Sipping all.

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:12.380
No wonder the unions are getting infiltrated.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:14.480
You should have spent the evening with your brother members.

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:14.960
I did.

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:16.900
We had more at the bingo than we had at the meeting.

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:18.900
Ah, disgraceful.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:21.940
I pride myself on the fact that I've never missed a union meeting.

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:24.370
Twelve years I've been treasurer of the railway union

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.270
and every member comes to every meeting.

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:28.150
With you as treasurer, I'm not surprised.

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:29.930
Are you trying to suggest that I...

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:33.090
Here, they smell nice.

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:34.970
I'll have a couple of them sausages for my breakfast.

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:36.190
Oh, I'm sorry, there's some more left.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:37.290
These are for Stan's lunch.

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:39.050
I don't like cold bangers, Mum.

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:40.530
Oh, you're not going to have them cold, love.

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:41.970
I'm putting them in the firmers.

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:47.520
How am I supposed to get them out there?

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:48.360
Oh, don't worry.

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:49.480
Pour them on a plate or something.

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:51.870
Well, have you got any bacon?

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:52.590
I'm afraid not.

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:54.650
He'll use that for Stan's sandwiches.

00:03:57.310 --> 00:03:57.890
Here, Harper.

00:03:58.230 --> 00:03:59.290
Try a bit of fried bread.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.840
Fried bread, that's no good for a working man.

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:04.620
Working man? You're a working man?

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:06.540
A booking clerk at Crossley Junction,

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:09.010
three trains a day, two of them cancelled.

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:12.640
The amount of work you get through, mate,

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:14.560
you could survive on a cream cracker.

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:18.080
Well, I suppose I can fill up with cornflakes.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:19.360
Hey, where's the milk, Mum?

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:22.500
Oh, dear, I am sorry. It's finished.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:24.380
Not Stan's lunch again.

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:27.340
Oh, no. Rusty's breakfast. Come on, Mum.

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:28.640
Yes, come on.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.580
You'll have to wait till the milkman comes.

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:32.860
Time for walking.

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:38.020
Morning, Mum.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:39.040
How are you?

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:41.820
Not very well. I had a terrible night.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:42.700
Oh, dear, I'm sorry.

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:44.080
Oh, God, here we go again.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:45.160
Morning, Stan.

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:47.920
Oh, come on, say good morning to your sister.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:49.660
Morning, Olive. Coughing better?

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:53.520
She had me awake all night with that chest of hers,

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:54.940
weaving and puffing away.

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:56.720
I've been in bed with a steam engine.

00:04:58.200 --> 00:04:59.320
Watch it, love, watch it.

00:04:59.420 --> 00:04:59.960
You'll burst your...

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:02.240
Stop fussing.

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:03.000
Well, it's murder, man.

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:04.220
Well, if can't help it.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:06.200
All this carry-on about her wheezes.

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:07.710
It's only when she breathes.

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:09.310
That's right, love.

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:10.450
You take the syrup.

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:11.210
It'll do you good.

00:05:11.730 --> 00:05:13.010
It's always the same when they were children.

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:15.690
You know, mate, you always have a fun weak chest.

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:16.350
That reminds me.

00:05:16.390 --> 00:05:17.750
Have you got your vest on?

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:18.290
Yes, I have.

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:18.710
Leave me alone.

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:19.890
There you are.

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:20.930
Now you've got a cough now.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:21.490
Come on.

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:22.830
You'd better have some of this creosote.

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:24.490
Creosote wipes out coughs.

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:25.870
It wipes out dry rot and all.

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:28.710
I don't want to take nothing back, mate.

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:29.170
I'm telling you.

00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:29.770
No-

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.520
I get poisoned enough from the cab fumes without having to take that.

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:34.580
And, God, look at the time I'll be late, Mum.

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:35.800
I'll have to borrow your bike, Olive.

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:37.860
Here, wait a minute, here's your lunch.

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:38.160
All right.

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:40.490
There's your sandwiches.

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:40.890
Good-bye, Mum.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:41.590
Your banners.

00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:42.150
Yeah.

00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:42.830
That's it.

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:43.790
And there's your tea.

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:44.150
Right, open up.

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:45.390
Oh, don't do that, it leaks.

00:05:45.890 --> 00:05:46.010
Oh, God.

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:47.290
That's it.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:48.340
Is that all, Mum?

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:48.860
I've got to go there.

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:49.360
Here, wait.

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:50.140
Here's your tea.

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:52.370
Oh, that and I drank that.

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:54.540
Only on the number 11 route, I've got nowhere to stop.

00:05:55.340 --> 00:05:57.020
There's a stop in the middle of the high street.

00:05:57.970 --> 00:05:58.870
I didn't mean that.

00:05:59.050 --> 00:05:59.970
I mean, if I drink too much...

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.020
liquid it goes right oh never mind

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:32.980
then, have you? Here comes our new clippy.

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:34.780
Oh, why don't you right say, son?

00:06:35.390 --> 00:06:36.630
Why don't you belt up, mate?

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:39.170
Yeah, come on, hurry up and sign in. We'll do it in a minute.

00:06:39.410 --> 00:06:40.090
Yeah, all right then.

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:43.640
Well, here we are. How are you, mate? How are you?

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:45.800
All right, mate. These new schedules are murder, aren't they?

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:48.620
Oh, murder. I don't know what they want to water them for.

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:50.510
Yeah, watch out. Here comes the Gestapo.

00:06:52.230 --> 00:06:54.530
You're not frightened of him, are you? I'm surprised at you, Jack.

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:56.060
Me, I'd... Oh.

00:06:58.570 --> 00:06:59.970
Get in the bus. I'm just getting in.

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:04.000
Don't go and put all that stuff in the cab like that.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:05.340
It could cause a nasty accident.

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:06.820
Put it on the stairs, Jack.

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:08.020
Come on, give us this.

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:12.710
Watch it, watch it.

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:13.820
You spill me sausages.

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:19.640
I suppose you have studied the new schedule, have you?

00:07:19.970 --> 00:07:21.790
You know the new stops and timing and stages

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:23.370
and turnarounds and change points and all that?

00:07:23.510 --> 00:07:25.810
Credit me with a bit of sense, will you, to mug it up?

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:27.020
I know the route.

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:28.700
Drive away.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:34.520
Hey Jack!

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:35.020
What?

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:35.720
Where are we going?

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:42.060
Cemetery gates via High Street.

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:38.090
What do you mean?

00:08:38.430 --> 00:08:40.510
You were due back at 11.33, you're 17 minutes late.

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:42.270
Yeah, I reckon it's very good.

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:44.800
The way I worked it out, I'd be 25 minutes late.

00:08:45.180 --> 00:08:46.300
These new schedules are murder.

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:47.400
Yeah, I'll stand. Easy lunch.

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:47.920
Thanks, Jack.

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:50.530
You know you're due out at 11.59, don't you?

00:08:50.690 --> 00:08:54.380
Hear that, 11.59, and the flipping canteen don't open till 12 o'clock.

00:08:54.520 --> 00:08:56.060
Where am I supposed to eat my grub?

00:08:56.330 --> 00:08:57.370
Where am I supposed to sit?

00:08:57.860 --> 00:08:59.220
You can use the branch provider, can't you?

00:09:00.670 --> 00:09:04.030
Charming, eh? Look, Jack, I've just come out of a warm cab.

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:06.180
I'm not eating my grub in this draughty shed.

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:07.240
Well, get back in the cab, then.

00:09:08.330 --> 00:09:10.060
Why didn't I think of that? Good idea, Jack.

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:11.600
Thanks, mate.

00:09:12.550 --> 00:09:15.880
The teeny-eats gone off the cab now.

00:09:16.060 --> 00:09:16.280
They are.

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:19.440
Charming, can't understand him.

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:27.470
Stop it, go on him.

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:29.290
I can't get my sausages out, mate.

00:09:35.500 --> 00:09:41.900
them out. Right. It's freezing

00:09:41.900 --> 00:09:43.870
cold in this cab. Well, turn the engine

00:09:43.870 --> 00:09:46.480
on and warm the cab up. Yeah, why didn't I

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:46.940
think of that?

00:09:55.990 --> 00:09:57.830
What's about the car? Do you tell the time now then?

00:09:59.230 --> 00:09:59.970
What's up there, boy?

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:00.840
What's it say?

00:10:01.460 --> 00:10:02.500
11.52, what?

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:04.140
You're not due out until 11.59.

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:05.960
I'm not going out to 11.59.

00:10:06.260 --> 00:10:07.720
What will you switch the engine on for, then?

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:09.920
Golden Air Force and Cabber.

00:10:10.430 --> 00:10:11.290
Switch that off a bunch.

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:12.380
What do you think it says here?

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:13.420
You're wasting the company's drill light.

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:13.880
Switch it off.

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:15.140
He's having his lunch in comfort.

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:15.800
Lunch?

00:10:16.100 --> 00:10:18.060
That's a cab for driving and not for eating in.

00:10:18.140 --> 00:10:19.040
Get out of there right away.

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:20.000
Come on, what do you think you're on, mate?

00:10:20.360 --> 00:10:21.900
That's a bus, not a mobile canteen.

00:10:21.940 --> 00:10:22.860
Get back in there, Stan.

00:10:23.290 --> 00:10:26.070
If the management won't open the canteen till 12 o'clock,

00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:27.110
you can stay now.

00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:29.980
You get done out there.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:35.760
at once i could report you know it could be uh two weeks suspension that's nice isn't it intimidation

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:43.580
yeah that's lovely take my notice then he can't intimidate you oh yes he can get down get back in

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:51.090
get down get in you get down get in you get out it's a matter of principle i better phone our union

00:10:51.090 --> 00:10:56.050
office now jack don't bring the union into this no you're right they never help right we've got to

00:10:56.050 --> 00:10:56.870
Let's settle this ourselves.

00:10:57.750 --> 00:10:59.130
Are you going to get out of there, aren't you?

00:10:59.210 --> 00:10:59.670
I won't.

00:10:59.690 --> 00:10:59.810
Dan!

00:11:00.060 --> 00:11:01.420
Don't you dare get out.

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:08.180
I'll go and see the general manager then, won't I?

00:11:14.010 --> 00:11:15.730
He's been told between his legs, eh, Jack?

00:11:15.890 --> 00:11:16.050
Yeah.

00:11:16.630 --> 00:11:17.350
Come on then, get out.

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:17.870
Eh?

00:11:18.430 --> 00:11:18.890
Get out.

00:11:20.560 --> 00:11:22.520
What are you talking about?

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:23.440
Come on, what do you think you're doing?

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:24.020
Get out!

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:25.340
You just told me to get back in!

00:11:25.420 --> 00:11:28.460
That was when the inspector told you to get out, but now I'm telling you to get out,

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:29.980
and I'm the shop steward, and I'm conv...

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:44.030
been in a meeting so get out. What about my lunch? New schedules if we have to suffer.

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:50.520
Brother Stan here has been threatened by an inspector. He has been intimidated for eating

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:54.600
his lunch in his cab because the management wouldn't open the canteen till 12 o'clock.

00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:59.480
I put it to you brothers. No canteen, no buses.

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:08.060
vote on it signifying the usual manner all those in favor we are unanimous simply

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:20.820
thank you right motion carried we are withdrawing our labor forthwith yeah can

00:12:20.820 --> 00:12:21.460
No more lunch now.

00:13:07.020 --> 00:13:07.620
Hi, Mum.

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:10.330
Oh, Stan.

00:13:10.900 --> 00:13:12.440
Yeah, what are you doing back so early?

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:13.620
Oh, what's happened?

00:13:13.840 --> 00:13:14.100
Nothing.

00:13:14.830 --> 00:13:15.510
I'm on strike.

00:13:16.010 --> 00:13:16.550
On strike?

00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:17.030
Yeah.

00:13:17.780 --> 00:13:20.280
Oh, so that's why there was no buses.

00:13:20.720 --> 00:13:22.860
Oh, really, I do think you might have told us.

00:13:23.100 --> 00:13:26.160
Me and Ollie, why we was walking two miles in the pouring rain.

00:13:26.480 --> 00:13:27.760
We couldn't tell you what happened so quickly.

00:13:27.960 --> 00:13:29.600
It's what's called a lightning strike.

00:13:29.820 --> 00:13:29.980
Nah.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:34.600
Ah, Stan, don't tell me you couldn't get the men to hold up the strike for your mum.

00:13:34.820 --> 00:13:36.520
They wouldn't hold it up for Frank Cousins' mum.

00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:38.440
Ah, well, the Dockers do.

00:13:38.970 --> 00:13:43.650
That one in 18, you know number 18, his mum, she always gets her meat in before the strike.

00:13:45.270 --> 00:13:47.940
And last year, her Christmas nuts also.

00:13:56.340 --> 00:13:57.460
Stan, do you hear that cough?

00:13:58.340 --> 00:13:59.760
I can hear it, sounds a lot better to me.

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:02.710
You'll feel much better after a cup of tea.

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:05.150
Now, look, stand, I bought some of those lovely fairy cakes.

00:14:05.470 --> 00:14:06.030
Get them out, will you?

00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:06.850
Just a minute, roughly.

00:14:07.190 --> 00:14:08.510
Are you all right, but not wet, eh?

00:14:09.270 --> 00:14:09.930
Wet? I don't know.

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:11.170
My mum hasn't had a look in the bag yet.

00:14:11.860 --> 00:14:13.120
Well, I'd say they're a little bit damp.

00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:14.900
Here.

00:14:17.270 --> 00:14:18.390
You paint the bags, had it, innit?

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:20.630
Hold on a minute.

00:14:20.730 --> 00:14:21.010
Hang on.

00:14:23.360 --> 00:14:23.600
Oh.

00:14:25.380 --> 00:14:26.360
Careful of the bulb.

00:14:26.900 --> 00:14:27.720
I don't know about that.

00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:28.300
I'll be looking at the barn.

00:14:28.360 --> 00:14:29.020
That's not bad, is it?

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:34.040
Well, it's no different than when you dip it in your tea.

00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:36.580
Don't talk like that.

00:14:36.760 --> 00:14:38.960
Well, let's face it, my matter, it ends up in your stomach, doesn't it?

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:40.680
Hey, come here.

00:14:42.070 --> 00:14:43.600
Oh, at the front door.

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:44.920
Is that you, Arthur?

00:14:45.420 --> 00:14:46.800
Yes, of course it's me.

00:14:47.080 --> 00:14:49.980
Arthur, there's a bus strike. Have you heard?

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:55.440
Yes, I have heard.

00:14:56.760 --> 00:14:59.800
You busmen ought to be shot striking on a wet day like this.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.440
Well, that's the best time to strike, isn't it?

00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:02.820
Rainy days and Christmases.

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:04.560
They've always taught us that.

00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:07.780
I'm soaked through to the skin.

00:15:07.900 --> 00:15:08.560
Oh, dear, I'm sorry.

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:09.220
You give it to me.

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:10.880
You are in a state, aren't you?

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:12.320
Oh, you're sopping.

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:13.160
Oh, now.

00:15:13.380 --> 00:15:14.140
Oh, dear.

00:15:14.520 --> 00:15:15.640
How did you get so wet?

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:18.600
Standing at a bus stop for an hour, waiting for a bus.

00:15:18.860 --> 00:15:20.040
Well, that was daft, wasn't it?

00:15:20.220 --> 00:15:21.820
Well, that was hard to know you were on strike.

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:24.260
Well, standing at a bus stop for an hour, nothing comes along.

00:15:24.420 --> 00:15:25.800
Blimey, you must have thought something had gone wrong.

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:26.960
Well, you lot run the buses.

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:28.400
We thought it was normal service.

00:15:30.860 --> 00:15:32.580
Are you a busman who are a lot of layabouts?

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:32.860
Yeah.

00:15:32.980 --> 00:15:34.640
I'd like to meet the bloke who started it.

00:15:35.010 --> 00:15:35.290
Would you?

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:38.740
Well, as a matter of fact, mate...

00:15:38.740 --> 00:15:40.240
Because when I do, I'll knock his block off.

00:15:40.280 --> 00:15:40.760
Who was it?

00:15:43.280 --> 00:15:44.000
Yeah, well...

00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:46.160
When I find out, I'll let you know.

00:15:47.030 --> 00:15:49.270
Your union had no right bringing you out on strike.

00:15:49.470 --> 00:15:50.490
They didn't. We did it ourselves.

00:15:51.080 --> 00:15:52.740
Oh, so he's unofficial.

00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:55.420
I suppose you know you'll get no strike pay.

00:15:56.530 --> 00:15:57.510
Is that right?

00:15:57.870 --> 00:15:58.910
No wages?

00:15:59.400 --> 00:15:59.980
Won't there be no money?

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:03.840
coming in? That's right, he could be out for months, not a single penny. Olive, have you

00:16:03.840 --> 00:16:07.720
heard that? Oh, Mum, Mum, don't worry. Yeah, look here, Stan, what are we going to do for

00:16:07.720 --> 00:16:12.980
money? We've got nothing behind us. I've just paid all the rates and there's the phone due

00:16:12.980 --> 00:16:19.040
and the HP. You have to tell the man you want to go back. Don't waste your breath, Mum.

00:16:19.180 --> 00:16:22.580
The runny telly will go back before he does. It wouldn't hurt you to pay a few instalments

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:26.270
on it for a change. And on the fridge, I've paid that for the last two years. Oh, we can't

00:16:26.270 --> 00:16:29.170
let them take the fridge back, can we? Oh, let them take it back. We won't have nothing

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:29.730
to put in it.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:31.620
We've got to all starve to death as far as he cares.

00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:34.460
Well, we'll just have to live on our office money, won't we?

00:16:34.870 --> 00:16:35.810
Then we will starve.

00:16:37.170 --> 00:16:39.750
No, it just means I shall have to start watching every penny.

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:41.350
Start? Blimey, you never stopped.

00:16:41.550 --> 00:16:43.370
Well, at least he's going to work tomorrow.

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:45.590
Yeah, more than you, sitting around doing nothing.

00:16:45.830 --> 00:16:47.390
I won't be sitting around doing nothing, mate.

00:16:47.970 --> 00:16:48.870
I'll be lying in bed.

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:51.920
Lying in bed? All day long?

00:16:52.040 --> 00:16:52.960
No, only till the pub's open.

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:54.670
It's great being on strike.

00:16:55.070 --> 00:16:55.870
No wonder it's catching on.

00:16:56.430 --> 00:16:57.290
Hang on, I'll get it off.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.540
Hello? No, it's me, Stan.

00:17:02.550 --> 00:17:04.920
Oh, hello, Jack. Strike committee.

00:17:05.240 --> 00:17:05.820
Big deal.

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:09.470
Yeah? Oh, God, no.

00:17:10.560 --> 00:17:12.430
When? What time?

00:17:13.850 --> 00:17:15.090
Yeah, all right. Yeah, all right, yeah.

00:17:15.870 --> 00:17:16.190
Tell her.

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:18.180
What's up, Stan?

00:17:18.560 --> 00:17:19.560
They won't be on picket duty.

00:17:19.960 --> 00:17:21.520
Oh, well, it's only right, isn't it?

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:23.340
Yeah, but I've got to be there at half past five in the morning.

00:17:23.540 --> 00:17:25.160
That means I'll have to be up at half past four.

00:17:26.010 --> 00:17:27.550
Hardly worth going to bed, is it?

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:29.970
Olive, I'll have to use your...

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:33.850
Oh, well, I shall need her bike to get to work meself, shall I?

00:17:33.970 --> 00:17:35.210
How am I going to get on picket duty?

00:17:35.770 --> 00:17:36.650
Up on a bus.

00:17:42.610 --> 00:17:43.970
Here, Jack, I'm fed up with this.

00:17:44.170 --> 00:17:47.170
We've been standing it for five hours and nobody's even tried to get in.

00:17:48.350 --> 00:17:49.850
They've not even tried to start up a bus.

00:17:49.950 --> 00:17:51.510
Oh, you never know what the management will get up to.

00:17:52.170 --> 00:17:53.090
Got to show them we're solid.

00:17:53.410 --> 00:17:53.970
I'm not all right.

00:17:54.090 --> 00:17:55.230
I can't even straighten me fingers.

00:17:56.920 --> 00:17:58.500
Here, when are we going to knock off a lunch?

00:17:58.840 --> 00:17:59.980
Knock off a lunch?

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:02.360
Look, we do an eight-hour shift, non-stop.

00:18:03.360 --> 00:18:04.480
Well, I'm standing here, come to your mother.

00:18:06.940 --> 00:18:08.600
Look, we don't want no interference from the women.

00:18:08.820 --> 00:18:10.420
She's probably passing. She'll be all right.

00:18:12.080 --> 00:18:13.820
I had to come see you were all right.

00:18:14.040 --> 00:18:15.120
I bought you a few things.

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:16.900
I'd go home before you and Mum, it turned half cold here.

00:18:16.960 --> 00:18:20.080
I know, that's why I bought you an extra pair of warm socks and hot water bottle.

00:18:20.480 --> 00:18:22.700
Yeah, and your mother is making us look ridiculous.

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:24.000
Yeah, she won't be wrong yet.

00:18:24.060 --> 00:18:27.080
Oh, here you are. Some nice hot tea and some warm bums.

00:18:27.560 --> 00:18:28.680
Some warm bums, lovely.

00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:29.900
Oh, that's very nice.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:30.280
Sure.

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:31.240
Don't eat no shit.

00:18:31.320 --> 00:18:32.380
You make yourself look ridiculous.

00:18:33.540 --> 00:18:37.760
I'm going to take you some cherry linters in case the cold goes down to your chest.

00:18:37.900 --> 00:18:38.360
I'll put it in your pocket.

00:18:38.360 --> 00:18:38.780
Hey, look, look.

00:18:39.330 --> 00:18:41.330
There's some brooks coming across the street with a camera.

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:44.500
I wonder what they want.

00:18:45.020 --> 00:18:45.220
Yeah.

00:18:45.920 --> 00:18:47.220
We are from the TV news.

00:18:47.280 --> 00:18:49.280
We'd like a few shots for tonight's programme, OK?

00:18:49.540 --> 00:18:50.980
Oh, yes, that'll be all right, yeah.

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:52.320
We need publicity.

00:18:52.520 --> 00:18:53.160
That's OK, isn't it?

00:18:53.320 --> 00:18:54.440
Yeah, I reckon it's all right, yeah.

00:18:54.660 --> 00:18:56.060
Yeah, I think you look a bit pale.

00:18:56.590 --> 00:18:58.030
Don't you think you ought to have some make-up on?

00:18:58.150 --> 00:18:58.790
Shut up, Mum.

00:18:59.090 --> 00:18:59.970
Well, they all...

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:08.510
do, the Queen, and Mr. Wilson. Well, he probably borrows Barbara Castle's powder puff. Well, I think

00:19:08.510 --> 00:19:13.230
you'll be all right. Well, wait a minute. I've got a bit of lipstick here. That'll help anyway. Come on.

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:19.930
No. Tony, and you might make me look a fool. Hey, listen. They're starting up one of the buses.

00:19:20.930 --> 00:19:24.030
They're going to take it through the bucket. Here, quick. We've got to stop them. Here, hold that, Mum.

00:19:24.290 --> 00:19:29.890
Hold this. What's going to do with this? Well, I don't want that. Here, Sam. Wait for me, Sam.

00:19:43.790 --> 00:19:47.690
She's speckless. They're bringing the bus out. Ruddy strike breakers.

00:19:48.490 --> 00:19:49.450
Scarf! Scarf!

00:19:50.810 --> 00:19:51.830
Black leg! Black leg!

00:19:51.930 --> 00:19:52.530
Look at her!

00:19:53.460 --> 00:19:54.300
Yeah, we'll have to stop it.

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:55.830
How are we going to do that, Jack?

00:19:56.050 --> 00:19:56.470
Lie down.

00:19:56.910 --> 00:19:57.210
Lie down?

00:19:57.390 --> 00:19:58.610
Yeah, lie down in front of the bus.

00:19:59.180 --> 00:19:59.380
Go in.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:01.280
No, you. Yes, you. Me.

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:02.100
Me?

00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:07.160
Just a minute, Jack. Hang on, hang on.

00:20:07.240 --> 00:20:09.390
I just thought of something. Why don't you lie down there?

00:20:09.510 --> 00:20:11.340
No, no. I'm the committee leader.

00:20:11.560 --> 00:20:12.920
I've got to negotiate with him.

00:20:13.360 --> 00:20:15.360
Come on, lie down. Quick, lie down

00:20:15.360 --> 00:20:17.520
before he gets by. I'll drive the lie down

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:19.580
off and it's gone by. Besides, he might not stop.

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:21.280
No, well, we'll get him for manslaughter.

00:20:21.960 --> 00:20:23.840
I'd love to see those inspectors inside.

00:20:24.080 --> 00:20:25.600
Yeah, and so would I. But he might not know

00:20:25.600 --> 00:20:27.620
how to drive that thing. Besides, I know that

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:29.340
bus is a dodgy crate. Yeah, come on, quick.

00:20:29.340 --> 00:20:29.920
Come on. Come on.

00:20:40.180 --> 00:20:41.120
You leave him alone.

00:20:41.540 --> 00:20:42.120
It's been raining.

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:43.120
He'll catch his death at school.

00:20:43.180 --> 00:20:43.860
Come on, come on.

00:20:43.920 --> 00:20:44.760
Cut all this time for him.

00:20:44.860 --> 00:20:45.180
Come on.

00:20:45.580 --> 00:20:45.880
Come on.

00:20:46.680 --> 00:20:47.780
Don't you kick my son.

00:20:48.020 --> 00:20:49.220
He ain't done you no harm, have he?

00:20:49.650 --> 00:20:49.890
All right.

00:20:50.070 --> 00:20:50.190
All right.

00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:51.610
That's all.

00:20:52.470 --> 00:20:53.490
Stay there all night for all I care.

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:56.140
I say, just a minute.

00:20:56.520 --> 00:20:57.340
Let's have a shot.

00:20:57.940 --> 00:20:58.160
All right.

00:20:58.240 --> 00:20:58.740
Now do you want me?

00:20:59.150 --> 00:20:59.350
Right there.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:02.040
I say, what's that red stain on your coat?

00:21:02.340 --> 00:21:02.780
What stain?

00:21:06.670 --> 00:21:07.770
Mum, it's blood!

00:21:08.430 --> 00:21:08.950
Are you sure?

00:21:09.250 --> 00:21:10.530
It's just what we wanted.

00:21:10.730 --> 00:21:11.650
We'll have a ball out now.

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:12.540
Blood!

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:13.650
You've been injured.

00:21:14.130 --> 00:21:14.830
Don't get up.

00:21:14.990 --> 00:21:15.470
Stay there.

00:21:16.220 --> 00:21:17.100
Are you all right, love?

00:21:17.180 --> 00:21:17.840
Are you all right?

00:21:17.940 --> 00:21:18.560
I don't know, Mum.

00:21:19.700 --> 00:21:20.080
One minute.

00:21:21.320 --> 00:21:21.840
No, don't panic.

00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:22.260
Don't panic.

00:21:22.700 --> 00:21:24.560
It's that rotten cherry syrup you've got for this morning.

00:21:24.740 --> 00:21:25.520
It's not a vodka bowl.

00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:26.120
Oh, Stan.

00:21:26.500 --> 00:21:27.620
Focus on the blood.

00:21:27.960 --> 00:21:28.800
Don't panic, Mike.

00:21:28.920 --> 00:21:29.440
It's a syrup cat.

00:21:30.380 --> 00:21:31.500
Blad, what is...

00:21:31.590 --> 00:21:34.430
Oh, oh, yes, yes, Blad, yeah.

00:21:34.690 --> 00:21:36.130
Oh, are you all right by that, aren't you?

00:21:38.950 --> 00:21:40.410
Time's very unsettled.

00:21:40.670 --> 00:21:42.550
And now the regional news.

00:21:42.810 --> 00:21:43.930
Hey, hurry up, Mum, I'm on.

00:21:44.090 --> 00:21:45.170
All right, I'm all right, I'm coming.

00:21:45.310 --> 00:21:46.330
Come on, I've got a chair here, sit there.

00:21:46.730 --> 00:21:47.310
That's it, sit there.

00:21:47.550 --> 00:21:49.330
I bet they won't even bother to show it.

00:21:50.260 --> 00:21:51.620
No, what's that then, eh?

00:21:51.740 --> 00:21:52.100
What's that?

00:21:52.840 --> 00:21:54.600
Hey, hey, look, Mum, that's me.

00:21:55.260 --> 00:21:56.940
Well, all you can see is your backside.

00:21:58.080 --> 00:21:59.600
Well, it's very nice.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:05.430
As the unofficial Luxton and District bus strike moved into its second day,

00:22:05.630 --> 00:22:07.370
there was drama at the bus depot

00:22:07.370 --> 00:22:10.290
when driver Stan Butler threw himself in front of the bus

00:22:10.290 --> 00:22:13.350
to prevent it being taken out and was slightly injured.

00:22:13.510 --> 00:22:14.710
What a ruddy fraud.

00:22:15.070 --> 00:22:15.250
Shush!

00:22:17.830 --> 00:22:18.770
Hey, is that me?

00:22:19.150 --> 00:22:19.830
Yes, love.

00:22:20.370 --> 00:22:22.270
Oh, something's gone wrong. My face looks all fat.

00:22:22.550 --> 00:22:22.790
Oh.

00:22:23.030 --> 00:22:24.730
That's cos your face is all fat.

00:22:24.890 --> 00:22:25.530
Ah, shut up.

00:22:25.830 --> 00:22:27.410
There's something wrong with a set, that's what it is.

00:22:28.290 --> 00:22:29.970
Ha-ha, that makes you look a lot better.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:30.580
Shut up.

00:22:30.880 --> 00:22:31.640
A smile, look.

00:22:32.100 --> 00:22:32.840
Oh, yes, you're smiling.

00:22:32.860 --> 00:22:33.760
Yes, have you got it here?

00:22:33.880 --> 00:22:35.240
Oh, yes, a lovely smile, that is.

00:22:35.820 --> 00:22:37.040
You shouldn't have bothered.

00:22:37.600 --> 00:22:41.340
I asked Dan Butler if he thought his courageous action was justified.

00:22:41.620 --> 00:22:42.280
A bitter ending.

00:22:43.190 --> 00:22:46.020
You know what, that's about it.

00:22:49.720 --> 00:22:51.420
Yeah, who's that stupid woman?

00:22:51.700 --> 00:22:52.180
It's you.

00:22:54.120 --> 00:22:55.800
Oh, yes, so it is, yes.

00:22:56.300 --> 00:22:59.030
And now some football.

00:22:59.270 --> 00:22:59.910
Well, alright.

00:23:00.120 --> 00:23:01.260
Burke, you made it yourself.

00:23:01.500 --> 00:23:02.220
What are you talking about?

00:23:02.540 --> 00:23:04.280
Oh, I think it was very nice.

00:23:04.700 --> 00:23:05.340
It's a good idea, really.

00:23:06.110 --> 00:23:08.330
It's a pity your teeth are so crooked, though, love.

00:23:08.650 --> 00:23:10.170
Well, didn't notice much, did it, ma'am?

00:23:10.290 --> 00:23:10.970
Well, I don't know.

00:23:12.300 --> 00:23:14.360
Do you think it would be too late to wear a brace?

00:23:16.750 --> 00:23:18.810
Well, you and your pals will have to give in now.

00:23:18.890 --> 00:23:20.890
The management certainly won't after that in a lot.

00:23:21.070 --> 00:23:22.290
Well, at least I've been on telly.

00:23:22.630 --> 00:23:23.710
So have the monsters.

00:23:24.200 --> 00:23:25.660
Oh, here, the buses are coming on.

00:23:25.700 --> 00:23:26.460
Look, the buses, look.

00:23:26.680 --> 00:23:27.220
Here we are.

00:23:27.650 --> 00:23:29.090
And here is the news, lad.

00:23:29.330 --> 00:23:29.970
Listen, we'll jump...

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:36.580
You've just heard that after a long meeting, and in view of the injury sustained by driver Stan Butler, the hero of the day,

00:23:37.080 --> 00:23:41.360
the management have agreed to the busman's demand in order to avoid further bloodshed.

00:23:41.480 --> 00:23:46.520
Oh, Stan, you've won, you've won, and all because of you they give in!

00:23:46.640 --> 00:23:50.260
Yeah! So I'm a burke, am I?

00:23:50.700 --> 00:23:53.520
Well, I'll tell you what, Arthur. I reckon from now on I can tackle anything.

00:23:53.780 --> 00:23:55.120
Well, you can start right away.

00:23:55.340 --> 00:23:55.720
What do you mean, Mum?

00:23:56.540 --> 00:23:57.440
Tackle the washing up.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:05.420
What does it matter, fellas? We've won, didn't we?

00:24:06.380 --> 00:24:07.600
We taught the management a thing.

00:24:07.680 --> 00:24:09.700
Yeah, now we know how to get what we want, don't we?

00:24:09.760 --> 00:24:10.060
Of course, yeah.

00:24:10.420 --> 00:24:11.400
Come on, Stan, come on, Jack.

00:24:11.660 --> 00:24:12.820
You'll do it out in two minutes. Get in the bus.

00:24:12.980 --> 00:24:14.440
Hold your hair on, hold your hair on.

00:24:14.710 --> 00:24:15.930
We're the bosses now, you know.

